## Docker

{% if choices.docker == "full" -%}
Mode: **everything in Docker**. `docker-compose.yml` has two services:

- `dev` (profile `dev`, image stage `dev` of `Dockerfile`): mounts the project folder at `/app`, keeps `node_modules` (root, `server/`, `web/`) in named volumes, runs as user `node`, publishes `APP_PORT` and `WEB_PORT` and sets `APP_HOST`/`WEB_HOST` to `0.0.0.0`. `docker compose up dev` runs `npm run dev` with hot reload; `docker compose run --rm dev npm …` runs any script. After changing dependencies run `docker compose run --rm dev npm install`.
- `app`: the production image (see below), `docker compose up --build app`.
{%- else -%}
Mode: **Docker to run the app**. Development happens on the host with Node.js (`npm run dev`); Docker builds and runs the production container.
{%- endif %}

- `Dockerfile` (multi-stage, `node:24-alpine`): builds the web app with all dependencies, installs only the server's production dependencies for the runtime image, which runs `node server/src/index.ts` as user `node`. `.env` is never copied into the image.
- `docker-compose.yml` reads `.env`: `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` ({{ project.slug }}) names the stack, `APP_NAME` is a build argument for the web build, `APP_PORT` is published, and `APP_HOST` is forced to `0.0.0.0`.
- **Data:** `DOCKER_DATA` in `.env` decides where containers keep the SQLite files (`/app/data`): {% if choices.data == "local" %}**`./data`** — the project's `data/` folder is mounted (current setting); set `DOCKER_DATA=data` to use a Docker volume instead.{% else %}**`data`** — the named volume `{{ project.slug }}_data` (current setting); `docker compose down -v` deletes it. Set `DOCKER_DATA=./data` to keep the files in the project's `data/` folder instead.{% endif %}
- Commands: `docker compose up --build{% if choices.docker == "full" %} app{% endif %}`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} logs -f`, `docker compose{% if choices.docker == "full" %} --profile dev{% endif %} down` (add `-v` to delete the volumes).
- The runtime image contains only `package.json`, `server/package.json`, `server/src`, `web/dist` and the server's production `node_modules`. When the server needs more files at runtime, add `COPY` lines to `Dockerfile` (and check `.dockerignore`). Runtime dependencies of the server must be in `server/package.json` `dependencies`.
{% endif %}
